  "scope": "Local macOS arm64 owned Chrome156.0.8078.48. Actual TLS WSS selected after bounded unreachable WT contact, two synthetic Opus microphone streams through the public typed browser SDK. No model/account/provider, PSTN, named remote, Linux, package or publication execution.",
  "finding": "The earlier zero-output WSS probe is resolved: Chrome received RTP but emitted no decoded samples when its remote receiver was connected only to Web Audio. An owned muted HTML audio element starts RTC decoding; the Web Audio graph retains audible volume and presentation control.",
  "implementation": [
    "BrowserRtcConnection.render owns the muted audio element with the original received track, starts play under the same bounded startup budget, and pauses/resumes it with its Web Audio graph. Resume shares one deadline across graph resume and element play.",
    "Startup/resume playback rejection reports media failure and closes the exact sink/graph. Deadline, abort, retirement and explicit close pause it and clear srcObject. Late play completion cannot reacquire a retired sink. Graph-close tasks remain joined by bounded SDK shutdown.",
    "The new owned Chrome audio test uses current invitation handles, two actual offers and explicit subscriptions; ordinary media control flows through the public SDK. Test observers only inspect decoded PCM/receiver sample counters. No fixture audio element supplies decoder startup."
  ],
